"""The M0 comparison harness: Qwen 2.1 edit output versus the Krea 2 configurations, on the same slots.

What it answers: is the Krea 2 path actually better than tool2's Qwen edits for this character, and which of the two
Krea 2 model shapes should the pipeline use? It cannot answer that by itself, so it produces the things a person
needs to answer it:

* the same fixed slot set generated by every method, at the same seeds;
* a contact sheet pairing slot x method side by side, with a 1-5 scoring form under each image;
* a CSV of those human scores, and an aggregate that turns them into one recommendation with its reasons.

It never trains. The seed LoRA it compares (`suamom_v1`) was trained by hand; choosing an epoch from an existing run
is an argument here, and training a new one stays the runner's job.

  python -m pipeline.experiment plan   --card experiments/suamom_card.json --out experiments/m0_suamom
  python -m pipeline.experiment run    --out experiments/m0_suamom
  python -m pipeline.experiment sheet  --out experiments/m0_suamom --serve
  python -m pipeline.experiment report --out experiments/m0_suamom
"""
